      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What would the actual effect on the audio be? Quieter based on camera distance?\n\nRight now when I'm recording a video in OBS I tell the software to capture the audio from the headphones and from the microphone. Unless you want to hear your own voice, like a speech jamming technique, you would want to get your voice filtered by VRChat a different way.\n\nFor a video capture directly by VRChat I could see it done, just add option to control volume of mic based on distance from camera, and maybe grab and decode the output from the voice chat codec instead of a good quality direct mic capture.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
